{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0546","billNumberShort":"H.B. 546","billNumberLong":"HB0546","fileNumber":"2026FL0740","shortTitle":"Public Lands Duty of Care Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"IVORYK","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Ivory, Ken","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses the jurisdictional management of public lands.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>asserts the state's jurisdictional interest in land controlled by the federal government under a proprietary interest;<hr><ltbullet>directs the Public Lands Policy Coordinating Office (office) to promote the state's jurisdictional interests on landscape-scale public lands; <hr><ltbullet>requires the office to:<hr><ltbullet1>identify and map landscape-scale lands in the state;<hr><ltbullet1>establish map layers for certain criteria on landscape-scale lands;<hr><ltbullet1> map a landscape public nuisance area on landscape-scale lands containing forested areas; and<hr><ltbullet1>report annually on the map to the Federalism Commission;<hr><ltbullet>requires the Division of Forestry, Fire, and State Lands to assist the office in identifying a landscape public nuisance area for landscape-scale lands containing forested areas; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Ryan C. Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"KLAFUGOEYI","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-11 09:14:42.790","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","par